{"title":"2023 BmMT Individual Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border: 1px solid #444; background: #fff; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 20px auto; font-size: 90%; line-height: 1.6; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n<div style=\"background: #e0dbff; padding: 12px; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid #444;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 110%; font-weight: bold; color: #4b3ba7;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_(Answer_Key)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual (Answer Key) (page does not exist)\">2023 BmMT Individual (Answer Key)</a></span><br />\n<span style=\"font-size: 95%; color: #6c5cb8;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">BmMT Resources</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Upload&amp;wpDestFile=2023_BmMT_Individual.pdf\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual.pdf\">PDF</a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 15px 25px 15px 25px;\">\n<p style=\"font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;\">Instructions</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">This test contains 20 short answer questions. All answers must be expressed in simplest form unless specified otherwise. Only answers written inside the boxes on the answer sheet will be considered for grading.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Each correct answer is worth 1 point. Each incorrect or blank answer is worth 0 points.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">No calculators are permitted.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">You will have <b>60 minutes</b> working time to complete the test.</li>\n</ol>\n<div style=\"text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; word-spacing: 2px;\">\n<p><a href=\"#Problem_1\">1</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_2\">2</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_3\">3</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_4\">4</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_5\">5</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_6\">6</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_7\">7</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_8\">8</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_9\">9</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_10\">10</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_11\">11</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_12\">12</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_13\">13</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_14\">14</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_15\">15</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_16\">16</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_17\">17</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_18\">18</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_19\">19</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_20\">20</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is 20% of 23 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is 23% of 20, compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pablo wants to eat a banana, a mango, and a tangerine, one at a time. How many ways can he choose the order to eat the three fruits?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f73d811eca6419d9c9a27423331d71ff06eb957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be 3 positive integers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/6535bafd572f3b644206fa3b27783a0555447bc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + \\frac{b}{c} = \\frac{11}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"39\" />, what is the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle has an area of 12. If all of its sidelengths are increased by 2, its area becomes 32. What is the perimeter of the original rectangle?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rohit is trying to build a 3-dimensional model by using several cubes of the same size. The model’s front view and top view are shown below. Suppose that every cube on the upper layer is directly above a cube on the lower layer and the rotations are considered distinct. Compute the total number of different ways to form this model.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Priscilla has three octagonal prisms and two cubes, none of which are touching each other. If she chooses a face from these five objects in an independent and uniformly random manner, what is the probability the chosen face belongs to a cube?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> be two congruent isosceles right triangles where line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are their respective hypotenuses. Connecting a line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> gives us a square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/5/2f504f4dcff47b737748f0d79f47fc39536e82e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACFD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> but with missing line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810aad7c62c4157f33b3d6d8d7a1f78cb4db3856.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC, AD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Instead, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are connected by an arc defined by the semicircle with endpoints <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db920c16c37f9ecd5503cc0b8f06f924bc6f9ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, what is the perimeter of the whole shape <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b12d9f695c68516cfa29c67dcc3703bdc2d3872a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCFED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" />?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two moles that live underground, and there are five circular holes that the moles can hop out of. The five holes are positioned such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6521ad84932f05bbfa1185b24d793813c7aefc2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are the centers of the circles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/6157d6ce02973817e2f8308883bb88755c47f14c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = 30\\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />, and congruent triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/9/8e91703e3671196130a25ab6a7c4986c4ea0cce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC, \\triangle CBD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are equilateral. The two moles randomly choose exactly two of the five holes, hop out of the two chosen holes, and hop back in. What is the probability that the holes that the two moles hop out of have centers that are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e3dd5df5a28a11d9fdad92c0d7677f6829e09eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15\\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> apart?\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Carson is planning a trip for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> people. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of cars that will be used and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of people per car. What is the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that there are exactly 3 possibilities for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94c45489bc9bbeae5ab98827205179e938f7c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, and exactly one person is left without a car?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Iris is eating an ice cream cone, which consists of a hemisphere of ice cream with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22ff7db3e755a8164f2344e0d3d84ea3a0fe93b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> on top of a cone with height 12 and also radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Iris is a slow eater, so after eating one-third of the ice cream, she notices that the rest of the ice cream has melted and completely filled the cone. Assuming the ice cream did not change volume after it melted, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As Natasha begins eating brunch between 11:30 AM and 12 PM, she notes that the smaller angle between the minute and hour hand of the clock is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d8911ed57672cebe73effdb50b99af8e45d12ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. What is the number of degrees in the smaller angle between the minute and hour hand when Natasha finishes eating brunch 20 minutes later?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />, Luke the frog starts at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />; there is food on points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and there are crocodiles on points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. When Luke is on a point, he hops to any of the five other vertices with equal probability. What is the probability that Luke will visit both of the points with food before visiting any of the crocodiles?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>2023 regular unit hexagons are arranged in a tessellating lattice, as follows. The first hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> (with vertices in clockwise order) has leftmost vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> at the origin, and hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a78e6b70b5c8d657720fb7406cf5e33b2295cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f63ee58ad120aa7d967debf149d0b5b5982dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> share edges <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> with hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d307bbd1badc9884ef8f01724a6e1cbf9e173a8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />, respectively. Hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c88df920a869d31db81a1ba7735837704b571ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> shares edges with both hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a78e6b70b5c8d657720fb7406cf5e33b2295cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f63ee58ad120aa7d967debf149d0b5b5982dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />, and hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6793fd92e76bd71b29a15ceeb25cb6c86eb84779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a342e12b9e348bc7c0c6e7e1b67f7dad901c2ab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> are constructed similarly to hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a78e6b70b5c8d657720fb7406cf5e33b2295cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f63ee58ad120aa7d967debf149d0b5b5982dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />. Hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a9968d230b2f992a30e3f4434434264cfb8e59dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38e80262d31068e6f3b3cd316bd3d0c79fb5d649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_{2022}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> are constructed following the pattern of hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de9ed85d67915f5218f23ba517a3f27fffc752d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_4, H_5, H_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. Finally, hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bcebd1e99e31356961f5bd37919bad1887270b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_{2023}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> is constructed, sharing an edge with both hexagons <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e54bc51da6103130223c3ad562c635aeee3416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_{2021}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/e/38e80262d31068e6f3b3cd316bd3d0c79fb5d649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H_{2022}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />. Compute the perimeter of the resulting figure.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:Missing_Diagram&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:Missing Diagram (page does not exist)\">Template:Missing Diagram</a>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Aditya’s favorite number is a positive two-digit integer. Aditya sums the integers from 5 to his favorite number, inclusive. Then, he sums the next 12 consecutive integers starting after his favorite number. If the two sums are consecutive integers and the second sum is greater than the first sum, what is Aditya’s favorite number?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The 100th anniversary of BMT will fall in the year 2112, which is a palindromic year. Compute the sum of all years from 0000 to 9999, inclusive, that are palindromic when written out as four-digit numbers (including leading zeros).\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6521ad84932f05bbfa1185b24d793813c7aefc2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, in that order, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ade6fba5778539a12863b1ca2852599a7f598fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = 2DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/7095ae12134c87c4a40c15917fdd7d1881d19a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/0/280aacc6974cad97f4d6bcb70a5edc6bc7cf5839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PE = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/753f18f2a94bd8de13c61fc43a12f4fd344ba25d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 8x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/a/b8a398d0346f785a4acfe718ef2710250ac209c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME = 9x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8fba2b0bcad1690b69a669265374b14ee06643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = 112$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, compute the sum of the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca7ebfe4cb06e20c204fa1dc02267597aad658cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />-plane is rotated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> about a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The resulting parabola has roots at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afae2c0f2b22fb6a5ad988d9ad4de951de80f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0864bc0f5dcd5cf4776f3b9f29ff4b11ef1153c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Susan has a standard die with values 1 to 6. She plays a game where every time she rolls the die, she permanently increases the value on the top face by 1. What is the probability that, after she rolls her die 3 times, there is a face on it with a value of at least 7?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a 6-digit number satisfying the property that the average value of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1959fb6c1c25367ebcc29e707f9c1a9ad259e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" /> is 5. Compute the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1959fb6c1c25367ebcc29e707f9c1a9ad259e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f8039a17007507e3599a6dd2efe10e9671ce4451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1, O_2, \\dots, O_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> be circles of radius 1 such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/f/22fee8432afef182522d8398a9420869d82da5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> but no other circles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6f63aa2266ef1b39b31386bd17b28e25faaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> but no other circles, and so on. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a circle that is externally tangent to each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac32366ded820ed3f1fddbc7a4da2ac15e76d0d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1, O_2, O_3, \\dots, O_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. Compute the radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2023 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:BmMT_Individual_box&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:BmMT Individual box (page does not exist)\">Template:BmMT Individual box</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">Berkeley Mini Math Tournament</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BmMT_Problems_and_Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"BmMT Problems and Solutions (page does not exist)\">BmMT Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">Mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018064700\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.063 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.101 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 627/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 149/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17175/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.931      1 -total\n 14.37%    2.576      1 Template:BmMT_Individual_box\n 13.68%    2.453      4 Template:Missing_Diagram\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37783:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018064700 an